Response: documented from human-service PATCH /orgs/audiences/{id}, which owns it; the gateway forwards it unchanged. Its full document: GET /v1/platform/services/human.","params":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"Audience ID","type":"string"}],"body":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"nlPrompt":{"type":"string","nullable":true}},"additionalProperties":false},"answers":[{"status":"200","description":"Updated audience","schema":{"truncated":true,"firstChars":"{"type":"object","properties":{"audience":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"orgId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"brandId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"nlPrompt":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"description":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"One-sentence summary of who THIS audience targets, distinct from the shared batch nlPrompt. LLM-generated at /suggest time. null for rows predating this field."},"provider":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"enum":["apollo","apify","crm",null]},"apolloAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Pointer to the faithful Apollo audience owned by apollo-service ('one filter vocabulary' Wave 2). Set for apollo audiences; null for apify (legacy) rows and pre-Wave-2 rows not yet backfilled. The faithful filters live in apollo-service; the `filters` field below is human-service's opaque cache of them."},"crmUploadId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"The ONE imported CRM source (crm-service upload id) this audience is bound to. When set, every CRM serve made under this audience is restricted to the people that came from that file, so several CRM audiences can coexist for one brand and each behaves as its own audience. null = unbound ⟹ the serve covers the brand's whole imported list (the pre-existing behaviour)."},"crmPeople":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"properties":{"signedUp":{"type":"boolean"},"replied":{"type":"boolean"},"reachableBy":{"type":"string","enum":["phone","email"]},"segment":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"A part of the brand's own CRM, as crm-service's PeopleSegment states it (passed through verbatim, validated by crm-service): dealStages [{stage, pipeline?}], dealStatuses, tags, reached / notReached (funnel steps), includeClients, includeOptedOut. Lists OR, keys AND; clients and opted-out people are out unless stated. Names come from crm-service GET /orgs/contacts/segments.","example":{"dealStages":[{"pipeline":"Sales Pipeline","stage":"Form Filled - No Appointment"}]}}},"description":"The PEOPLE-pool filter this CRM audience is bound to: every serve draws from the brand's merged people (everyone its connected tools know, one row per human) who match it, instead of from imported files. null = not people-bound (file-bound via crmUploadId, or the whole imported list)."},"crmPeopleByStage":{"type":"array","nullable":true,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"pipeline":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"stage":{"type":"string"},"served":{"type":"integer"},"remainingSendable":{"type":"integer"},"totalSendable":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["pipeline","stage","served","remainingSendable","totalSendable"]},"description":"A people-bound CRM audience whose segment names dealStages: crm-service's counts per stated stage (same snapshot as Size / Remaining). Entries overlap when a person holds deals at two of them. null otherwise."},"offerId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The offer (Org > Brand > Offer > Campaign) this audience belongs to — an id owned by brand-service. An audience is assembled for one distinct thing the brand sells, so it is scoped to that offer rather than to every offer of the brand. null = no offer stated ⟹ the audience is brand-wide, the pre-existing behaviour."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["suggested","active","paused","archived","deprecated"],"descripti